# A 5-by-5 grid with four options per vertex and bounded integer costs.
# The grid retains small separators. Every edge has its own dense factor.
# Costs sampled with Python random.Random(9), unary entries in node order
# from range(5), then edge entries from range(9). Visit edges by source,
# horizontal before vertical, and sample each table in row-major order.
# From the repository root:
# ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bucket --numthreads=16 -Werror --verbose examples/pbqp/14_bucket_beats_bnbopt.pbqp
# ./build-clang-modules/pbqp --solve=bnbopt --numthreads=16 -Werror --verbose examples/pbqp/14_bucket_beats_bnbopt.pbqp
# Both solvers prove COST 93. The induced width is 5.
# Clang 21 Release, Intel Core Ultra X7 358H, 16-thread limit.
# Median of five alternating CLI runs including startup:
# bucket 7.22 ms; bnbopt 4.86 s.

